1
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:07,438
Code generation is solved. But nobody lets an AI delete code,

2
00:00:07,518 --> 00:00:11,550
and nobody lets an AI ship to production alone. So we put one on probation.

3
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:17,073
This is Tallybook, an invoicing app with years of debt:

4
00:00:17,153 --> 00:00:21,729
dead API versions, stale flags, unused packages.

5
00:00:21,809 --> 00:00:27,550
Every line costs build time, image size, cold starts, and carbon.

6
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:34,706
Every night a census reads Cloud Run's request logs

7
00:00:34,786 --> 00:00:43,304
and files a grave for each piece of code that production proves is dead.

8
00:00:43,384 --> 00:00:47,550
Evidence, not guesses.

9
00:00:48,050 --> 00:00:53,550
Undertaker is a GitLab Duo flow that can only delete.

10
00:00:54,050 --> 00:01:01,550
It digs the grave, opens a minimal MR, then a coroner step attacks its own work.

11
00:01:02,050 --> 00:01:05,044
It can't merge. A deterministic gate decides,

12
00:01:05,124 --> 00:01:08,550
and a new agent starts on Assisted: a human approves.

13
00:01:14,650 --> 00:01:28,150
Every change ships through a canary and a soak.

14
00:01:28,650 --> 00:01:33,150
Survive production, earn trust, per code zone.

15
00:01:33,650 --> 00:01:40,150
Supervised: it merges itself; I approve production.

16
00:01:40,650 --> 00:01:48,150
Two graves later, it's Hands-off in the legacy zone.

17
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:54,150
Now nobody's watching. It buries the CSV export: zero hits in seven days.

18
00:01:54,650 --> 00:01:59,968
But our bookkeeping partner calls it once a month.

19
00:02:00,048 --> 00:02:04,150
The canary soak catches the 404,

20
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:13,283
traffic rolls back, the commit is reverted,

21
00:02:13,363 --> 00:02:16,750
and Undertaker loses 40 points.

22
00:02:17,250 --> 00:02:22,750
Back to Assisted. That grave is never touched again.

23
00:02:23,250 --> 00:02:28,750
Every MR is measured in gCO₂e per thousand requests with the SCI spec.

24
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:32,483
Plan, create, verify, package, secure, release, configure, monitor, govern:

25
00:02:32,563 --> 00:02:34,750
all nine stages, on GitLab and Cloud Run.

26
00:02:38,850 --> 00:02:42,178
Autonomy you can earn, and lose.

27
00:02:42,258 --> 00:02:44,350
Probation.
